    p("18:91","known-content",[("onun yanında",5),("kini",4)],"Bima ladayhi identifies what was with him in the encompassing-knowledge clause. Expose the relative object ending instead of a full duplicated nominal phrase; the preceding Turkish bilmek frame absorbs the preposition.")
    d("18:91:4","Restore the nominal-relative contribution in the known content without adding an unsupported physical instrument.")
    p("18:93","hardly-understanding",[("neredeyse ",11),("hiç ",10),("anla",12),("ma",10),("yan",12)],"La yakaduna yafqahuna describes scarcely understanding. Turkish neredeyse hiç anlamayan retains the inherited degree reading while exposing negation at la rather than copying neredeyse into it. No extra ability suffix is introduced.")
    d("18:93:10","Restore negative scope separately from the nearness auxiliary; the selected scarcely-reading follows the supplied English and inherited Turkish sense.")
    d("18:94:2 18:94:3 23:20:5","Retain the individually inspected proper-name views: ey Zülkarneyn has the same shared surface with vocative/name components exposed, and Tur-i Sina'dan keeps the source suffix on the final component. No missing named referent or different source location is inferred.",True)
    c("19:8","how-existence",{3:"nasıl",4:"olur"},"Anna asks how and yakunu supplies being/existence. Restore the predicate rather than copy benim, which belongs to the following li.")
    d("19:8:4","Restore the existence predicate in the question about having a son.")
    p("19:34","disputed-relative",[("hakkında ",8),("şüphe edip ayrılığa düş",9),("tük",7),("leri",9)],"Alladhi fihi yamtaruna identifies the disputed referent. Expose the relative ending and retain about it separately. This local grammatical split does not uniquely settle the larger attachment of qawl al-haqq.")
    d("19:34:7","Restore the relative contribution without treating alladhi as a duplicate preposition.")
    d("19:43:5 19:74:4 19:79:7","Individually retain the supplied nominal frames: some knowledge coming, quantified earlier generations, and extended punishment as a direct object. Min identifies content or class in each local construction; an added physical-source ablative is not mandatory.",True)
    p("19:44","rebellious-state",[("isyankâr",9),("dır",7)],"Kana asiyyan characterizes the devil as rebellious; restore an ongoing nominal attribute instead of a one-off completed act isyan etmiştir. The copula is exposed at kana.")
    d("19:44:7","Restore the rebellious-state predication while retaining its relation to the Most Gracious at the intervening location.")
    p("19:61","promise-assurance",[("yerine gelecek",11),("tir",9)],"Kana ... matiyyan assures fulfillment of the promise. Turkish future-assurance predication carries -tir; expose it rather than copy the promise noun into kana.")
    d("19:61:9","Restore the predicate support without treating the divine promise as a ceased past event.")
    d("19:63:8","Man kana taqiyyan is rendered by the nominal relative korunanlara; Turkish incorporates the characterization in that inflected relative rather than a separate finite copula. Retain the contextual view without adding a past-only condition.",True)
    p("19:64","not-forgetful",[("ve ",15),("unutkan",18),(" değil",15),("dir",16)],"Wa-ma kana rabbuka nasiyyan denies forgetfulness. Expose conjunction, negation and copula at their actual source words rather than copying Rabbin into kana.")
    d("19:64:16","Restore the negative nominal predication without implying the Lord later became forgetful.")
    d("19:93:1","In kullu man ... illa ati is universal negative-exception restriction: all will come as servants. Turkish hepsi ... gelecektir with ancak carries that universality; do not add a second independent negative that denies their coming.",True)
    d("20:71:16 20:73:10","Retain the separately inspected manner/content frames: min khilaf is çapraz and min al-sihr identifies the magic they were forced into. The Turkish direct-object magic phrase does not require a new physical-source suffix.",True)
    d("20:97:7","An taqula is the appointed speech content of the lifetime consequence. Turkish sen ... diyeceksin realizes it as a finite quoted-speech frame; retain its contextual an view without duplicating a nominal saying predicate.",True)
    p("20:97","devoted-relative",[("tap",22),("tığın",19)],"Alladhi qualifies the claimed deity with the relative devoted-to predicate. Expose the relative ending at alladhi and the worship/devotion root at akifan, preserving persistence at zalta.")
    d("20:97:19","Restore the relative qualification rather than copy the separate persistence adverb into alladhi.")
    p("20:98","negative-relative",[("ol",0),("ma",5),("yan",4)],"Alladhi la ilaha illa huwa is a relative qualification containing negative existence. Turkish olmayan exposes -yan as the relative contribution and -ma as negation; ol is support for the nominal Arabic clause.")
    d("20:98:4","Separate the relative and negative contributions without altering the exclusive deity statement.")
    p("20:114","before-completion",[("tamamlan",11),("ma",10),("dan",8),(" önce",9)],"Min qabli an yuqda is before completion, not so that it may be completed. Restore the positive temporal nominal tamamlanmadan önce; -ma is nominalization in this before construction, not a denial of completion.")
    d("20:114:8","Restore the time boundary and remove the inherited purpose misreading diye / tamamlansın.")
    p("20:115","covenant-addressee",[("Adem",4),("'e",3)],"Ila Adama marks the addressed recipient in the inherited instruction/covenant frame. Expose the dative rather than duplicate the fully inflected name at ila.")
    d("20:115:3","Restore the recipient suffix while preserving the separate covenant/instruction predicate.")
    d("21:2:1","The no-new-reminder-except-listening-at-play construction is rendered by Turkish her ... dinlerler. Its universal restriction is already overt across the clause; retain the contextual negative view rather than add a second negation denying all listening.",True)
    p("21:24","earlier-people",[("benden önce",15),("kilerin",14)],"Man qabli is those before me. Expose the nominal-person/genitive ending at man while qabli supplies the before-me relation; man here is not the preposition min.")
    d("21:24:14","Restore the relative people contribution without confusing Arabic man with min.")
    d("21:47:14 31:16:7","Min khardal identifies the grain as mustard. Turkish hardal danesi is a compound with no independent source suffix; retain the kind relation rather than invent an origin clause.",True)
    p("21:52","devoted-personal-relative",[("tap",11),("tığ",8),("ınız",9)],"Allati antum ... akifuna qualifies the statues to which they are devoted. Expose the relative ending, personal agreement and devotion predicate independently; Turkish tapmak is the inherited contextual devotion reading.")
